<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<embarkmodules>
  <!-- Declares Vixy_NameFlavourModule to character creation. The game resolves the class by name
       and instantiates it, the same way a blueprint's <part Name="..."> resolves to a class, so
       nothing here reflects into anything.

       No <window> element, deliberately. A window would add a page to character creation, and
       this module has no UI - it reads an option and replaces one string. Modules are enabled by
       default (AbstractEmbarkBuilderModule._enabled starts true), so a windowless one is active
       and receives boot events without appearing anywhere. -->
  <module Class="QudExpandedCE.Vixy_NameFlavourModule" />

  <!-- Reads the sultan history after the game generates it and answers one of its loose ends. #731.

       A SEPARATE module from the one above, and that is the point rather than tidiness.
       Vixy_NameFlavourModule adds itself to info.modules early so the name re-roll reaches it, and
       EmbarkBuilder later does embarkInfo.modules.AddRange(...) with no duplicate check - so that
       module is in the list twice and its handler fires twice per boot event. Its two handlers
       survive that because one sets a property and the other returns a name. Appending history
       events does not survive it: run twice, it doubles everything. This module never joins the
       list early, and carries a game-state guard as well. -->
  <module Class="QudExpandedCE.Vixy_HistoryModule" />
</embarkmodules>
